---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Operations Management & People Leadership" current="/operations-leadership/" description="Richard Allen's operations and people-leadership experience across SaaS support, workforce operations, reporting, process improvement, coaching, strategic goal alignment, project coordination, and warehouse management.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Operations Management & People Leadership</div><h1>Build structure around people, priorities, workflows, data, and change.</h1><p class="lede">My operations experience spans team leadership, workflow coordination, reporting, coaching, strategic goal alignment, process improvement, service delivery, cross-functional work, and earlier warehouse and supply operations.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="stats-grid compact-stats">
    <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">21</span></div><div class="metric-label">people in the documented HawkSoft Customer Service group during Team Lead-era scope</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">400+</span></div><div class="metric-label">position records managed across multiple OHA divisions</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">20+</span></div><div class="metric-label">recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports maintained for leadership</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">~20</span></div><div class="metric-label">people typically supervised in earlier Aramark warehouse operations</div></article>
  </div>
  <div class="operating-model" aria-label="Operations leadership model">
    <div><span class="model-dot teal-dot"></span><strong>People</strong><small>Coach, communicate, develop</small></div>
    <div><span class="model-arrow">→</span></div>
    <div><span class="model-dot blue-dot"></span><strong>Workflow</strong><small>Clarify priorities and coverage</small></div>
    <div><span class="model-arrow">→</span></div>
    <div><span class="model-dot gold-dot"></span><strong>Measures</strong><small>Make work visible through reporting</small></div>
    <div><span class="model-arrow">→</span></div>
    <div><span class="model-dot violet-dot"></span><strong>Improve</strong><small>Fix friction and reinforce better ways of working</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Operations in practice</div><h2>Leadership with the operating system attached.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Not just supervising people—also improving the information, goals, procedures, coordination, and routines around the work.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">LEAD</div><h3>Support-team leadership</h3><p>At HawkSoft, progressed from Team Lead to Customer Support Manager and led customer-support operations across a documented 21-person Customer Service group. Work included hiring and disciplinary authority, performance management, quality review, workflow coverage, escalations, stand-ups, and one-on-one coaching.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">ALIGN</div><h3>Cascading SMART goals</h3><p>Used a cascading SMART-goal structure to create clear line of sight from company priorities through leadership, departments, teams, and individual employees. Combined SMART-goal coaching with operational objectives, key results, and performance measures so individual work supported broader organizational goals.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">FLOW</div><h3>Service workflow & coordination</h3><p>Monitored support coverage, escalations, team activity, and service needs while coordinating with development and other teams around releases, troubleshooting, customer migrations, and operational priorities.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">DATA</div><h3>Management reporting</h3><p>Analyzed support and phone-system data in Excel, using pivots and KPI-style reporting to turn large raw exports into information leadership could use for decisions and follow-up.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">400+</div><h3>Workforce operations at scale</h3><p>As Position Manager / Operations & Policy Analyst II at Oregon Health Authority, managed 400+ position records, organizational charts, vacancy and position trackers, and 20+ recurring or ad-hoc workforce reports.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">X-FN</div><h3>Cross-functional coordination</h3><p>At OHA, coordinated with Recruiting, HR, Classification & Compensation, Budget, DEI, and leadership. At HawkSoft and The Kotter Group, work repeatedly connected customer-facing teams, software, training, documentation, and operations.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">OPS</div><h3>Administrative operations</h3><p>At Marion County Health & Human Services, coordinated scheduling, intake, service coordination, reporting and data accuracy, onboarding, cross-training, and multiple competing priorities in a confidential environment.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">SOP</div><h3>Process governance & consistency</h3><p>At Oregon Employment Department, led/co-led a department-wide SOP modernization and governance program: inventorying and updating 25+ legacy procedures, coordinating contributors across roughly 10 functional groups, standardizing templates and review controls, and centralizing a library that ultimately identified, created, and collected 100+ SOPs.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">$1M+</div><h3>Warehouse & supply operations</h3><p>Earlier at Aramark Foodservice, typically supervised about 20 people while overseeing purchasing and supply duties, receiving, storage, distribution, shipping, sanitation, and driver or small-fleet activity for more than $1 million in inventory annually.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><strong>Leadership style:</strong> create line of sight between organizational priorities and individual work, make performance visible, coach people toward stronger results, and improve the system around them so good work is easier to repeat.</div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
